# The Founderizer release public keys (PRODUCT.md 4.2 and 4.3): the keys that sign a release for every fleet.
#
# One base64 line for each 32-byte Ed25519 public key, and lines that start with # are for the reader. No private
# half is on any server or hub: the approve key is in the Secure Enclave of the owner's Mac and signs only after the
# owner's Touch ID, and the spare is in the owner's own password manager. A fleet can check a release and can never
# make one. A fleet that takes each release early trusts the keys of early-key.pub as well.
#
# **This file holds a set, and every key in it is trusted.** That is what makes a key replaceable: the release
# that brings the next key is signed with the key it replaces, every release after it is signed with the new one,
# and a fleet that skipped the release in between still carries a key that checks both. PRODUCT.md 4.3, "How a
# signing key is replaced", says how a key is brought in, how long both stay here and when the old line goes.
# At most four lines; a line that is not a 32-byte key makes the whole file carry nothing, because a key file that
# is half read is a mistake and a fleet that cannot say which keys it trusts takes no release.
#
# The lines, in order: the website's old key, which signs nothing after this release and which the next release
# removes; the approve key; the spare, which signs the release that replaces a lost key.
Rx2H3IQWLleJlIx+4x2ckg0JN4d+CGjfF0Zkeon6vmg=
